{
  "question": "What's the copay tier for Trulicity?",
  "status": "answered",
  "assumption": "Assuming NY Medicaid (coverage question, no program named). Part D tiers and VA formulary status aren't in the searchable documents.",
  "answer": "Assuming NY Medicaid: NYRx doesn't use copay tiers. The PDL only lists preferred or non-preferred status.\n\n- Trulicity is **Preferred** in the GLP-1 Receptor Agonists – Type 2 Diabetes class (PDL revised 9/14/2026).\n- The class has clinical criteria (CC). Confirm an FDA-approved or compendia-supported, Medicaid-covered indication.\n- PA is required if the patient is on a GLP-1 and a DPP-4 inhibitor concurrently.\n- The PDL is marked BLTG for Trulicity.\n- The PDL footer says \"Preferred as of 10/22/2026\". That date is still upcoming as of today (10/14/2026).\n\nThe documents don't give a copay amount or tier. I found no Part D formulary tier for Trulicity.",
